    "body": "La Liga giants Barcelona have been forced to sweat over the status of another leading member of the club’s first-team ranks for their upcoming meeting with Sabah. This comes amid the understanding that Joan García is not a certainty to play his part. Hansi Flick’s troops are primed to kick their Champions League campaign back into gear on Wednesday evening, courtesy of a trip to Azerbaijan to face the aforementioned Sabah. The Blaugrana will head into the fixture sans the services of the likes of Andreas Christensen, Rodri and Lamine Yamal. And as alluded to above, Flick and co. could yet be forced to make do without the contributions of their first-choice option between the posts in Baku, too. As per a report from Mundo Deportivo , Joan García finished Sunday’s win over Villarreal with pain in his knee, with it therefore concluded: ‘The goalkeeper is experiencing discomfort that improves with rest and will need to be assessed in the coming hours to determine whether he is fit to play in Baku against Sabah or if it is preferable to rest him.’ Conor Laird – GSFN",
